  "page_gates": "CONTRIBUTIONS are one schedule over pp2-4: p2 carries the header + 27 rows, p3 is the continuation (32 rows, no header), and p4 is the schedule's blank remainder carrying its own printed section total in a 'Sum' row - '$7,570.00'. The 57 rows reproduce it to the cent as a MONETARY sum with the two IN-KIND rows excluded, and it equals the cover's cumulative contribution figure. EXPENDITURES are one schedule over pp5-6: p5 prints the boxed 'Total amount of expenditures $8,628.89' above its grid and carries 22 rows, p6 is the continuation (12 rows) and prints its own 'Total $8,628.89' row under the grid; the 34 rows reproduce both to the cent and match the cover. NO specimen rows on this filing (a filer-built spreadsheet, not the county blank form). A SECOND, INDEPENDENT GATE closed on BOTH sides: the cover's CURRENT-REPORT column (contributions $1,750.00, expenditures $346.76) is exactly the sum of the rows dated after the pre-election cutoff - contributions dated 11/2/22 and later sum to 1,750.00, expenditures dated 11/1/22 and later sum to 346.76 - which also fixes the ledger's GRAIN as CUMULATIVE and independently proves the amount column is paired with the right rows.",
