  "withheld_rows": {},
  "notes": "Eve Furse, County Clerk, 2022 Post-Election. 6 pages, filer-built typed spreadsheet. THE SOURCE IS NOT A FLATBED SCAN: every ledger page is a PHOTOGRAPH of the printed sheet, taken at an angle in landscape orientation, with the camera's shadow across the right third, page bow, and bleed-through from the sheet behind visible on p4. That is a source property the briefs do not list and it has three consequences worth recording. (1) rowbands detects ZERO horizontal rules on pp2, 3 and 4 and only junk on pp5-6, so both sides ship on force_declared frames. (2) THE FILER'S SHEET PRINTS ITS RIGHT-HAND COLUMNS ABOUT ONE ROW HIGHER THAN ITS LEFT-HAND ONES - the Amount cell of a row sits roughly one row-pitch above that row's Date/Name, and the Zipcode about half a row above; the same offset is visible in the COLUMN HEADER itself ('Amount' prints higher than 'Date'). A naive read pairs each donor with the previous row's money. The pairing here is BY ORDER and it is established, not assumed: the counts match column for column (27 names / 27 addresses / 27 zips / 27 amounts on p2; 32 / 32 / 32 / 32 on p3), every zipcode matches its own row's city (Seattle 98109, New York 10026, Peoa 84061, Oakley 84055, SLC 84102/84103/84105/84106/84108/84109/84110/84111/84116, Draper 84020, Coalville 84017, Henefer 84033, Francis 84036, Kamas 84036, Midway 84049), Pat Christensen appears on BOTH p2 and p3 with the same address and zip, three tight crops at the top, middle and bottom of p2 and p3 show a full aligned row (Franci Eisenberg / P.O. Box 1503 Park City / 84060 / $100.00 and Philip Furse / 8 Blossom Ln, Manchester-by-the-Sea, MA / 1944 / $150.00), and finally BOTH sides pass a second arithmetic gate on the cover's current-report column, which a one-row amount shift would break. (3) The declared frames are fitted to the DATE/NAME line of each row - donor identity - so a resolved box shows the donor and address; because of the printed offset the Amount at the far right of that same box is the NEIGHBOURING row's, which is why the amount assignment rests on the arithmetic above rather than on a single crop. The frames are joint fits across each side's two pages (contributions: p3 rows are bands 1-32, p2 rows are bands 6-32, worst-case residual 0.91pct on a 2.42pct box; expenditures: p6 rows are bands 1-12, p5 rows are bands 12-33, worst-case residual 0.61pct on a 2.39pct box) because the two photographs of a side are at slightly different scales (measured pitches 2.47 vs 2.42 and 2.33 vs 2.43 pct) and only one frame per side can be declared. NOT REDACTED: unlike the other 2022 filings in this chunk, the county left this filing's Mailing Address column intact, so donor_city/donor_state are read from the page; street addresses and PO boxes were discarded at read time and never written. Two donors' address cells are honestly EMPTY (Summit County Dem. Party, Anonymous) - left empty by the filer, not redacted. Escalations: 3 tight crops (p2 mid-page, p2 tail block, p3 row 21) to settle the column-offset question."
